[Music]  nasa's ingenuity helicopter could make  its second trip above mars as early as  thursday monday's historic first flight  came after years of work by nasa  engineers to overcome  unprecedented challenges jonathan  vigliotti has more on the flight and  what it could mean  for the future of space exploration  this is the video nasa engineers waited  more than  six years to see monday ingenuity  lifted off the dusty surface of mars the  helicopter's own camera  captured a stunning picture of its  shadow the flight was brief less than 40  seconds long  and at low altitude about 10 feet but it  was more than enough to make it the  first  earthly aircraft to ever fly on another  planet  we have done it this is the first time  i've been able to say we've done it  with mars sitting 178 million miles away  from earth  project manager mimiang and her team had  to wait more than  three hours until nasa's mars  reconnaissance orbiter  passed overhead and relayed the data  back to earth  altimeter data confirmed  that ingenuity has performed its first  flight  an incredible feat considering mars is  mostly carbon dioxide atmosphere  is only around one percent as thick as  earth's the equivalent of altitudes  three times higher than mount everest  when things work  it looks easy i would like to take this  opportunity to remind how difficult it  is to fly a rotor crop at mars  the team plans four more flights over  the next two weeks  the hope that future helicopters could  one day serve as scouts for rovers  and eventually astronauts on the red  planet  for cbs this morning jonathan bigliotti  los angeles  it's a little machine and it's only a 10  foot flight but mars is 180 million  miles  exactly it looks like a mosquito but to  make a mosquito fly 108  million miles away so exciting job well  done nasa we're excited

